---
import Marketing from "../layouts/Marketing.astro";
import "../styles/home.css";
---

<Marketing
  title="Alkemyst — your local deck laboratory"
  description="Track Arena games, keep every deck version, and explore mana, equipment and tutors with seeded Rust simulations. Open source. Local-first."
>
  <section class="hero wrap" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
    <p class="eyebrow">
      <span aria-hidden="true">●</span> LOCAL-FIRST · OPEN SOURCE · IN DEVELOPMENT
    </p>
    <h1 id="hero-title">Brew with evidence.</h1>
    <p class="hero-copy">
      Your decks, your games, your next experiment. A local Magic: The Gathering lab for turning
      “what if?” into a question you can measure.
    </p>
    <div class="hero-actions">
      <a class="button primary" href="/download/">
        Preview status
      </a>
      <a class="button secondary" href="/docs/">
        Read the docs <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
      </a>
    </div>
    <p class="hero-note">
      Built for Arena constructed. Powered by Rust. Your library stays on your machine.
    </p>
    <figure class="product-view">
      <div class="window-chrome" aria-hidden="true">
        <span></span>
        <span></span>
        <span></span>
        <small>Alkemyst · Lab</small>
      </div>
      <img
        src="/images/desktop-lab.png"
        width="1440"
        height="1050"
        alt="Alkemyst Lab with a public Boros example deck, configurable trial count, tutor assumptions, and joint equipment goals."
        fetchpriority="high"
      />
      <figcaption>
        The working Lab interface with a public example deck. The model’s boundaries stay visible
        beside the experiment.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </section>
  <section class="story wrap" aria-label="From your last game to your next brew">
    <article class="story-row">
      <p class="section-number">01 / REMEMBER</p>
      <div>
        <h2>Keep the deck you actually played.</h2>
        <p>
          Arena capture preserves available game history and the submitted deck version. Edit your
          next brew without rewriting the past. Partial captures and unknown results stay clearly
          marked.
        </p>
        <a href="/docs/guides/tracking/">
          How tracking works <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </article>
    <article class="story-row">
      <p class="section-number">02 / EXPERIMENT</p>
      <div>
        <h2>Ask a more useful question.</h2>
        <blockquote>
          “With these tutors and mana costs, how often can I have two Equipment in play and one
          attached to an attack-ready creature by turn five?”
        </blockquote>
        <p>
          Run seeded Monte Carlo experiments and exact draw calculations. Compare curve and source
          counts. See sample sizes, uncertainty, legendary duplicate bricks, and the interactions a
          model does not support.
        </p>
        <a href="/docs/guides/analysis/">
          Read the analysis assumptions <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </article>
    <article class="story-row">
      <p class="section-number">03 / CONNECT</p>
      <div>
        <h2>Give your agent a local workbench.</h2>
        <p>
          Connect your own MCP-compatible agent to search cached cards, inspect history, compare
          versions, and run the same Rust experiments. Agent edits create new versions of your deck.
        </p>
        <a href="/docs/guides/mcp/">
          Connect through MCP <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </article>
  </section>
  <section class="community wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">A COMMUNITY LAB</p>
    <h2>Build your own better brew.</h2>
    <p>
      Alkemyst is Apache-2.0 software, built around a maintained Rust simulation engine. Help
      improve the models, add supported interactions, or make the app easier to use.
    </p>
    <div class="hero-actions">
      <a class="button primary" href="https://github.com/ebursztein/alkemyst">
        Explore the source ↗
      </a>
      <a class="button secondary" href="/docs/guides/development/">
        Start contributing
      </a>
    </div>
    <p class="fine-print">
      No accounts or cloud deck storage. Public card metadata and images need internet when fetched.
      In-app AI chat and preview installers are still being built.
    </p>
  </section>
</Marketing>
